# Most of what is here is deployed to a Linux controller: shell scripts, the
# Python boot-environment helper, systemd units and udev rules. A CRLF checkout
# breaks all four - the kernel refuses a `#!/bin/sh` shebang with a carriage
# return on it, and udev takes that return as part of the rule. Keep line
# endings LF regardless of the platform doing the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
